menu "gPlug-mini"

config GPLUG_SIM_METER
    bool "Simulated meter data (never ship)"
    default n
    help
        Feeds the aggregator from an embedded capture instead of the meter UART.
        Selected by building with sdkconfig.sim.defaults. A production image must
        never have this set; CI verifies that by inspecting the built binary.

comment "Network — empty by default, so a device provisions itself"

# These are EMPTY on purpose, and a shipped image must keep them so.
#
# FR-SUP-09 requires the device to treat SSID, passphrase and broker host as
# required and enter Provisioning when any is absent. A build that carries
# credentials makes them never absent, so the portal is unreachable and eleven
# provisioning requirements are dead code in the field. That is what this
# project shipped until 2026-08-05: `default "gplug-bench"`, which would have
# sent every deployed device looking for a workbench.
#
# A bench run that wants to skip provisioning builds with
# sdkconfig.bench.defaults, which fills them in. The convenience belongs to the
# bench, not to the product.

config GPLUG_WIFI_SSID
    string "WiFi SSID"
    default ""
    help
        Empty ships. A device with no stored configuration and no built-in
        credentials enters Provisioning on first boot, which is the intended
        behaviour (FR-NVS-02, FR-SUP-09).

config GPLUG_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "WiFi password"
    default ""

config GPLUG_MQTT_URI
    string "MQTT broker URI"
    default ""
    help
        Entered at the portal. §9.3 lists broker host and port among the
        configuration the portal collects.

endmenu
